#. y1:english="I'm into {MS:0}perfume||lately.\nMy room's overflowing with perfume.||Do you have any recommendations,\nKazuma-san?\nReally?{MS:1}{MS:0}||You mean I'm like a Parisienne?\nStop f{MS:0}lattering me,||Kazuma-san!\nI'm not. It's just...\nSpeaking of Paris, they say it's||a \"city of...\"\nWhat was it?\nNo, that's n{MS:0}ot it.\nIt's not? Sorry.\nYeah, that's it{MS:0}!||You're so smart, Kazuma-san!❤\nI try.\nIt's the City of Glamour.||Everyone's so stylish.\nI love Paris.❤\nOne d{MS:0}ay||I'll become a Parisienne!\nI'm sure.\nNo, wait{MS:0}.{MS:1}||I think that's Rome.\nRome's not in||France, is it?\nRome is in Italy.\nSee? Wrong then!||What was Paris called?\nOh, no!||Now I won't be able to sleep tonight.\nR{MS:0}eally?\nYeah.\nHey, that reminds me, Kazuma-san.\nThe other day I watched this really old||DVD called \"Roman\" something.\nThe actress in it||was really cute,\nbut the actor||wasn't really my type.\nI wonder if all||Italian guys are like that.\nActually, I don't think he was an Italian...\nI don't think I could fall in love||with someone like that.\nNot even cologne?\nIn that case,||I'll pick some out for you.\nI've never bought cologne before,||so it'll be something new for me.\nThanks. Don't buy me perfume, okay?\nOkay!"
