#. y1:english="...That's what it means{MS:0}, right?\nYeah, probably.\nDespite my appearance, I do have a sense||of justice. I can't stand young people who\ndon't give up their seats to old people||on the train. It makes me so mad.\nI just go up to them and punch them.\nThat reminded me...\nWhat? How'd {MS:0}you know?\nReally{MS:0}?||Was he okay?\nYeah, he was really thankful.\nGood, but you know,\nall the other people around||just pretended they didn't see him.\nI started to cry while I was helping him up.\nThat was sweet of you.\nHehe.❤{MS:0}That makes me feel good.\nHmm, you do, {MS:0}huh?\nYep, from the colour of hostesses' underwear||to shady deals in town.\nWow, you really do know everything.\n...\nThat's not {MS:0}my fault, right?\nThere's so many people out there that just||need to be punched!\nDon't you think so?\nYeah. I do.\nWhen I was a kid...||It just wasn't like that...\n(Sounds like it's gonna be a long story...)\nNot just {MS:0}young people, though.\nThose normally quiet old guys that get drunk||and those old women that won't wait in line.\nBut there are some good kids out there too,||you know?\nYeah, there are.\nYou can't put all kids into one category and||just say \"young people these days...\"\n(I think I stepped on a land mine...)"
