#. y1:english="...You know, \"{MS:0}Kazuma-san\" is||an unusual name.\nYou don't hear it very often.\nYeah, maybe.\nThe people you work with||never forget, huh?\nWell, I don't work with you,||but I'll never forget. Haha.\nBy the way, what is||your job, Kazuma-san?\nReally? {MS:0}No job?||That's cool, though.\nWhat is?\nThat you don't have a job,||but you can still go to clubs like this.\nIt means you have income without||having to work, right?\n...which means you're\na rich playboy.||Aren't you?\nHmm{MS:0}...\nSo you don't||deny being a playboy. Haha.\nI didn't say that.||I, uh...\nWhat are you {MS:0}embarrassed about?\nYou're acting like a guy whose girlfriend||found out he was cheating on her.\nYou're a serious kind of guy,||aren't you, Kazuma-san?\nLook, you even stopped||drinking...\nReally? {MS:0}Just to see me?||Stop it!\n...that kind of makes me happy...\nYou {MS:0}wouldn't?||You can't trick me!\nI'm not trying to.\nOkay. {MS:0}I believe you.||Let's talk some more, okay?\nAnd I'll just make sure||you're not lying.\nThat's acceptable, right?\nYeah, okay.\nHaha{MS:0}ha.\nYou're just full of lies,||aren't you, Kazuma-san?\nYou're {MS:0}a Yakuza, aren't you?||Don't deny it!\n...How did you know?\nEveryone said it||when you came in.\nThey said \"He's a Yakuza, so||don't be rude to him.\"\nOh. I see.||I'm not a Yakuza anymore, though.\nReally? {MS:0}You quit?\nIt kind of suits you, though.||Yakuza...\nA no nonsense Yakuza.\nI kind {MS:0}of||like that...\nHaha.{MS:0}||Just as I thought!\nHaha!\nWhat's so funny?\nYou think it's funny that a Yakuza||would come here?\nNo!||I'm just laughing that my first\nimpression was true.\nI'm good at guessing the occupation||of first time customers.\nI just knew you were||a freelancer.\nFreelance, huh?||That's a nice way of putting it.\nYou're {MS:0}handsome, though,||so I wasn't sure.\nBut my instinct was right!||Being able to tell\nso many things on the first meeting||is kind of like fortune telling, right?\nI like the word\n\"fortune\"\n..."
